    "q-39728": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39728",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $u$ and $\\text{Span}{w}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The distance between the vector $u$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{w}$ is given by $‖u-\\overset{^}{u}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{u}$ in the orthogonal projection of $u$ onto $\\text{Span}{w}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $u$ onto $\\text{Span}{w}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,u & =\\frac{w\\cdot u}{w\\cdot w}w \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 6}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}w \\\\  & =\\frac{8+2+4+6}{4+1+4+1}w \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10}w \\\\  & =2w \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u-\\overset{^}{u}‖ & =\\sqrt{({u}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{1})^{2}+({u}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{2})^{2}+({u}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{3})^{2}+({u}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-4)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(-2-(-4))^{2}+(6-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+0+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39728-a",
