    "q-86750": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86750",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-7{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-7{x}_{3})-3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot (-4)+(-13)\\cdot (-7)+1\\cdot (1)}{(-4)^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{132}{66}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
